      "widgets_values": [
        "4K MASKED EDITOR \u2014 HOW TO USE\n\n1. Choose or upload the finished image in LOAD 4K IMAGE.\n2. Right-click that node \u2192 Open in MaskEditor. Paint WHITE only over pixels that should change. Save to node.\n3. Replace the EDIT PROMPT with what must exist inside the mask.\n4. Queue the workflow. The edited crop is stitched back at the exact input dimensions.\n\nCRITICAL MASK RULE FOR HANDS\nMask the fingers and palm, plus only a very small amount of wrist. Leave the watch/bracelet, most of the forearm, elbow and surrounding scene unmasked as structural anchors. Crop and Stitch automatically adds context around your mask; you do not need to paint a large context blob.\n\nExamples:\nHAND: The same raised hand remains attached to the visible wrist and makes a two-finger peace sign...\nSMILE: The same woman's face and identity with a relaxed natural closed-mouth smile...\nREMOVE PERSON: The caf\u00e9 wall, chairs and pavement continue naturally through the masked region...\n\nDENOISE GUIDE\n0.55\u20130.65 subtle face/expression edit | 0.68\u20130.78 hand reconstruction | 0.85\u20131.00 object/person replacement."
      ],
      "title": "START HERE \u2014 mask and prompt instructions",
      "color": "#243",
      "bgcolor": "#465"
    },
